[{"id":92672,"sender_id":13,"sender_full_name":"Tim_Porter","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/f5067a77bfb4640f798f193b25d43eba?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/9-nLab-Technical-Matters/topic/Is.20the.20nLab.20down.3F/near/92672\">#7</a> Is the nLab down?</p>","timestamp":1626773389,"subject":"Is the nLab down?","stream_id":9,"display_recipient":"nLab Technical Matters","reactions":[]},{"id":92674,"sender_id":13,"sender_full_name":"Tim_Porter","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/f5067a77bfb4640f798f193b25d43eba?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/9-nLab-Technical-Matters/topic/Is.20the.20nLab.20down.3F/near/92674\">#8</a> It was down for a few minutes and now seems to be working again.</p>","timestamp":1626773599,"subject":"Is the nLab down?","stream_id":9,"display_recipient":"nLab Technical Matters","reactions":[]},{"id":92675,"sender_id":11,"sender_full_name":"Urs","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/b00d1ee17463af676c78974439b92471?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/9-nLab-Technical-Matters/topic/Is.20the.20nLab.20down.3F/near/92675\">#9</a> I notice that this happens more frequently lately (in the last few weeks, I think) that the <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">n</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.4306em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">n</span></span></span></span>Lab becomes unresponsive for a few minutes, a couple of times per day. Usually it’s back after cooking a pot of coffee (this to indicate the time scale, not to suggest a causation). But I hope it is not a sign of a general problem creeping up…</p>","timestamp":1626774199,"subject":"Is the nLab down?","stream_id":9,"display_recipient":"nLab Technical Matters","reactions":[]},{"id":92683,"sender_id":237,"sender_full_name":"Richard Williamson","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/b90dbe6063b47a44f7308efebb6ade2b?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/9-nLab-Technical-Matters/topic/Is.20the.20nLab.20down.3F/near/92683\">#10</a> Yes, there has been a deterioration in performance over the last few months. I believe that the current implementation for how edits are handled is reaching its limits. I am working on the AWS move, and unfortunately we’ll just have to hold out until that’s in place, and hope that things don’t get too much worse.</p>","timestamp":1626783978,"subject":"Is the nLab down?","stream_id":9,"display_recipient":"nLab Technical Matters","reactions":[]}]